# gRPC Requests
# Demonstrates gRPC calls with the JetBrains HTTP Client syntax: GRPC host:port/package.Service/Method
# Requires grpcurl: brew install grpcurl
# All examples use grpcb.in — a free gRPC testing service with server reflection
# (plaintext on port 9000, TLS on port 9001).

@grpcHost = grpcb.in:9000

### List the services (no method in the target)
GRPC {{grpcHost}}

### Unary call
GRPC {{grpcHost}}/hello.HelloService/SayHello

{
  "greeting": "Zed"
}

### Unary call over TLS (grpcs://)
GRPC grpcs://grpcb.in:9001/hello.HelloService/SayHello

{
  "greeting": "TLS"
}

### Send metadata (headers become gRPC metadata)
GRPC {{grpcHost}}/grpcbin.GRPCBin/HeadersUnary
authorization: Bearer my-secret-token
x-request-id: zed-123

### Use a host from http-client.env.json
GRPC {{grpc_host}}/addsvc.Add/Sum

{
  "a": 2,
  "b": 3
}

### ── Streaming ───────────────────────────────────────────────

### Server streaming — messages show when they arrive
GRPC {{grpcHost}}/hello.HelloService/LotsOfReplies

{
  "greeting": "stream"
}

### Client streaming — write one JSON message after another
GRPC {{grpcHost}}/hello.HelloService/LotsOfGreetings

{ "greeting": "Ada" }
{ "greeting": "Grace" }
{ "greeting": "Linus" }

### Bidirectional streaming — sends all messages, then reads the replies
GRPC {{grpcHost}}/hello.HelloService/BidiHello

{ "greeting": "one" }
{ "greeting": "two" }

### ── Directives ──────────────────────────────────────────────

### Timeouts (seconds, or a number with ms / s / m)
# @timeout 5
# @connection-timeout 2
GRPC {{grpcHost}}/addsvc.Add/Concat

{
  "a": "gRPC",
  "b": " Zed"
}

### Use a .proto file in place of server reflection
# @proto ./proto/hello.proto
GRPC {{grpcHost}}/hello.HelloService/SayHello

{
  "greeting": "proto file"
}

### ── Response capture ────────────────────────────────────────

### Capture values from the response
GRPC {{grpcHost}}/hello.HelloService/SayHello

{
  "greeting": "capture"
}

> {%
  client.global.set("grpc_reply", response.body.reply);
  client.global.set("grpc_status", response.status);
%}

###

### Use the captured value
GRPC {{grpcHost}}/hello.HelloService/SayHello
x-previous-reply: {{grpc_reply}}

{
  "greeting": "{{grpc_reply}} (status {{grpc_status}})"
}

### ── Errors ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Non-OK status (NOT_FOUND)
GRPC {{grpcHost}}/grpcbin.GRPCBin/SpecificError

{
  "code": 5,
  "reason": "this resource does not exist"
}
